    <string name="score_explorer_info_disclaimer_title">Disclaimer</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_limits_body">The past doesn\'t guarantee the future. KOSPI history only starts in 2021 and its first year is a burn-in period. Scores with few sample days can have very unstable averages.</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_limits_title">Limitations</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_method_body">Only days whose score exactly matches the one you picked are used — no interpolation. We collect the returns after those days and show the average plus the 10th (pessimistic) and 90th (optimistic) percentiles. Horizons are 21/63/126/252 trading days for S&amp;P 500 and KOSPI, and 30/90/180/365 calendar days for Bitcoin.</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_method_title">How it\'s calculated</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_sample_body">One day that hit the score is one sample. Consecutive days each count separately, so their windows can overlap. Treat fewer than 5 sample days as reference only.</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_sample_title">What counts as a sample</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_source_body">S&amp;P 500: CNN Fear &amp; Greed Index × S&amp;P 500 close (2011–) · KOSPI: our KOSPI Fear Index V2 × KOSPI close (2021–) · Bitcoin: alternative.me index × BTC price (2018–)</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_info_source_title">Data sources</string>
    <string name="score_explorer_lock_body">See how the next 1–12 months played out after days that hit any score, from the historical low to the high — real data, no guesswork.</string>
